    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC successfully triggered the vulnerability. The crash confirms exactly the analysis:\n\n- **Crash location**: `cbor_get_uint16` at `libcbor/src/cbor/ints.c:24` — a 2-byte read from a 1-byte heap allocation\n- **Root cause**: `fu_coswid_read_version_scheme` in `fu-coswid-common.c:108` calls `cbor_get_uint16(item)` on a CBOR uint item that has `CBOR_INT_8` width (1 byte allocated), because the code only checks `cbor_isa_uint(item)` without verifying the integer width is `CBOR_INT_16` or wider\n- **Trigger**: A uSWID firmware blob containing a coSWID CBOR map where the `version-scheme` tag (14) has a small uint value (encoded as CBOR_INT_8)\n\nThe 34-byte PoC consists of a valid 25-byte uSWID v3 header followed by a 9-byte CBOR map `{1: \"test\", 14: 1}`.",
